nts\nDepartment News\nDepartment Calendar\nEvents\nColloquium & Dissertations\nDarwin Day\nEarthstock\nDepartmental Resources\nAI & Technology Policy\nField Safety Equipment\nMore\n\u00d7\nSearch\nSearch\nCollege of Arts and SciencesDepartment of Ecology & Evolution\nHome\nAbout Us\nDepartment Leadership\nDiversity Statement\nFacilities\nGiving to E&E\nContact Us\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nFaculty Labs\nPublications\nPeople\nFaculty & Staff\nE&E Alumni\nJoin Us\nAcademic Programs\nAdmissions & Financial Support\nPh.D. Program\nPh.D. Admissions\nProgram Roadmap\nProgram Goals & Student Life\nTuition and Funding\nM.A. Program (Closed for 2027-2028)\nM.A. Admissions\nProgram Roadmap\nProgram Goals & Student Life\nTuition and Funding\nUndergraduate Programs\nEcology and Evolution Specialization\nEnvironmental Biology Specialization\nHuman Evolutionary Biology\nUndergraduate Resources\nEcoEvo Society\nUndergraduate Research Opportunities\nSpotlight\nAdvising\nNews & Events\nDepartment News\nDepartment Calendar\nEvents\nColloquium & Dissertations\nDarwin Day\nEarthstock\nDepartmental Resources\nAI & Technology Policy\nField Safety Equipment\nDepartment of Ecology & Evolution\nAcademic Programs\nTuition & Funding | Ph.D. Ecology & Evolution\nTuition & Funding\nFull-time doctoral students in the Ecology and Evolution Ph.D. program receive comprehensive\nfinancial support, including full tuition and fee coverage, health benefits, and competitive\nstipends.\nAssistantship Stipends & Support\nDoctoral support is provided through Research Assistantships (RA) or Teaching Assistantships\n(TA):\n12-Month Research Assistantships (RA): Minimum $40,667 over 12 months for 12-month appointments.\n9-Month Teaching Assistantships (TA): Paid at $30,000 over the 9-month academic year ($15,000 per semester). Over the three summer months,\nadditional funding is available through summer research appointments, teaching appointments,\nor federal work-study.\nHealth Benefits: All supported students receive a generous New York State health insurance package.\nApplicants are strongly encouraged to discuss funding plans, particularly summer funding,\nwith potential advisors.\nFellowships & Grants\nAdditional university-wide fellowship opportunities can supplement assistantship support,\nincluding:\nGraduate Council Fellowships\nW. Burghardt Turner Fellowships\nNSF Graduate Research Fellowships: Eligible domestic students (most entering students who have not completed a Master's\ndegree) are strongly encouraged to apply for an NSF Graduate Research Fellowship (GRFP).\nThese awards provide three years of stipend support, educational allowances, and supercomputer\naccess.\nImportant Funding Policies\nNew York State Residency Note: Domestic non-NY resident Ph.D. students with tuition scholarships must establish\nNew York State residency during their first year. Tuition scholarships are limited\nto in-state tuition starting in the second year. Details and instructions can be found\non the Bursar\u2019s Website.\nFooter\nDepartment of Ecology & Evolution\n650 Life Sciences Building | Stony Brook, NY 11794-5245\nPHONE: 631-632-8600 | FAX: 631-632-7626 | EMAIL: ecoevo_office@stonybrook.edu\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["College of Arts and Sciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/cas/"], ["Department of Ecology & Evolution", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/index.html"], ["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/index.html"], ["About Us", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/index.html"], ["Department Leadership", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/leadership.html"], ["Diversity Statement", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/diversity-statement.html"], ["Facilities", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/facilities.html"], ["Giving to E&E", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ecoevo/about-us/g